Playing nh 3.0 PL 3 (provided by kevins@cie.uoregon.edu) on msdos 3.3,
I came across a similar situation:

A archeologist named jones died while _dragging_ a ball & chain.
His remains are later found by a priest.  The ball, chain, and ghost-pile
are all separate:
	|..........|
	|...0......|
	|...._%....|
	|..@.......|

While looking (via ':') the iron ball (I have _not_ touched it!) I see:
	a heavy iron ball (chained to you)	same as above

Curiosity aroused, I then went to check out the chain:
	a iron chain

which I was able to pickup as a regular object!  I dropped the chain and 
went back to the iron ball, picked it up (expecting it to become magically
chained to me), but though it listed as "chained to me", I dropped it and
walked away free!

I then saved the game, and came back later to continue playing.

When I saved, the iron chain and ball were in different room from my character.
However, when I took my first step after restoring, my priest moved
(as is normal), but the so did the iron ball (half way across the screen!)
(It was being dragged through some kind of dungeon worm-hole/space-vortex! :-)
After one more step, it appeared beside me and from then on behaved as a 
normal chained-to-you iron ball.

Comments:
1. In a way, this is almost appropriate behavior for a iron ball in a 
   ghosts' pile.  Perhaps it should be made official?

2. I don't want to open yet another can of worms like the current food/eating
   debate, but shouldn't the iron ball be CHAINED to the corpse?  So if I
   pick up the ball I get:
	x - a heavy iron ball (chained to an archeologist corpse named Jones)
   (carried away? who me? :-)

